# ULTRON AIR API — repository ignores
#
# THE .env LINES ARE THE IMPORTANT ONES.
#
# .env holds live Gemini and Sarvam API keys plus the shared access token.
# Committing it publishes working credentials to anyone who can read this
# repository, and git history keeps them even after a later deletion —
# rotating every key would then be the only real remedy.
#
# Commit .env.example. Never commit .env. Set the real values as environment
# variables in the Railway dashboard instead.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules/

*.log
npm-debug.log*

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
